From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Builder <builder@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hdmitx: require the S7D SCMI PLL reference

Linux 6.12 can disable boot-enabled SCMI clocks during the unused-clock
sweep. The S7D HDMI driver is modular and probes after that sweep, but its
device-tree node does not name the HDMI/eARC PLL reference. It consequently
programs the HDMI PLL while its 24 MHz reference is disabled and the PLL can
never lock.

Make the reference mandatory on S7D and enable it before allocating or
initialising the HDMI instance. Report and propagate lookup, probe-defer, and
enable failures instead of continuing into a silent PLL timeout. Other SoCs
retain their existing clock handling.
---
--- a/common_drivers/drivers/media/vout/hdmi_tx_connector/hdmitx_drv.c
+++ b/common_drivers/drivers/media/vout/hdmi_tx_connector/hdmitx_drv.c
@@ -688,6 +688,7 @@ static int amhdmitx_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	int r, ret = 0;
 	struct device *device = &pdev->dev;
 	struct device *dev;
+	struct clk *hdmi_pll_ref;
 	struct hdmitx_common *tx_comm;
 	struct hdmitx_hw_common *hw_comm;
 	struct hdmitx_tracer *tx_tracer;
@@ -708,6 +709,13 @@ static int amhdmitx_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	HDMITX_DEBUG("chip_type:%d chip_name:%s\n",
 		chip_data->chip_type,
 		chip_data->chip_name);
+	if (chip_data->chip_type == MESON_CPU_ID_S7D) {
+		hdmi_pll_ref = devm_clk_get_enabled(device, "hdmi_pll_ref");
+		if (IS_ERR(hdmi_pll_ref))
+			return dev_err_probe(device, PTR_ERR(hdmi_pll_ref),
+				"failed to enable HDMI PLL reference\n");
+	}
+
 	/* allocate address space */
 	tx_comm = chip_data->hdmitx_ops->alloc_instance(device);
 	if (!tx_comm)
